sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch05-09> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Surface tension governs form only where surface energy is a large fraction of total energy, so it determines the forms of minute organisms and of the small cells of larger organisms, while the general forms of large organisms are due to other, non-molecular forces.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Surface tension governs the forms of small organisms and cells, not large organisms";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter V, “The Forms of Cells”; topic “Size limits of surface-tension control”. Scope: organisms and cells across sizes"
}
